**/.git
**/node_modules
.nx/cache

# AOS bus, agent configuration and code graph: never sent to a builder
# (SEC-05). **/ on every line: a pattern without it only matches at the
# context root (packages/twenty-agent-skills/.mcp.json was the real,
# confirmed miss that a root-only `.mcp.json` left uncovered).
**/.aos
**/.codegraph-aos
**/.claude
**/.dispatch-bodies
**/.mcp.json

# Real dotenv files at any depth (.env, .env.local, .env.production, the
# twenty-server .env.test/.env.e2e-testing-server test fixtures, deploy/local/.env,
# etc.). Docker does not apply a simple pattern recursively
# (https://docs.docker.com/build/concepts/context/), hence **/ on both lines.
# Only the explicit, secret-free *.env.example templates are re-included so
# the Dockerfile's directory COPYs still carry them.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# AOS-CRM local profile: deploy/local/privacy.env (CRM-003) is a non-secret,
# versioned, reproducible profile, not credentials -- it is excluded here
# only because the Dockerfile's build does not need it, not for secrecy.
deploy/local/privacy.env
